+# CTG-0001 — catálogo inicial do corpus `law/`
+
+**Papel:** Architect (Constituição, Artigo 6).
+**Rodada:** R-0019.
+**Status:** contrato fechado para transcrição em TASK-0002 e TASK-0003.
+
+## 1. Limites e taxonomia
+
+Este contrato destila o corpus já publicado; não cria regra de produto, papel,
+estado, prazo ou valor. O catálogo de cliente abaixo é a proposta M2 e só se
+torna taxonomia resolvida após o binding DEVAI do `adopter-policy.json`:
+
+| Classe               | Domínios                                    |
+| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
+| Cliente, proposta M2 | `INF`, `EST`, `CH`, `OPS`, `PORTAL`, `DASH` |
+| Core já declarado    | `SEC`, `AUTH`, `DATA`                       |
+
+`law/policy/adopter-policy.json` terá `schemaVersion: "1.0.0"`,
+`policy_id: "detran-law-corpus"`, `policy_version: "1.0.0"` e apenas a
+extensão adotadora `domains.client` com os seis códigos da proposta M2. Ele não
+altera `glob_guards`, `thresholds` ou `scorecard_na`.
+
+## 2. Catálogo fechado de invariantes
+
+Cada item transcrito em `law/invariants/<id>.json` usa
+`schemaVersion: "1.0.0"`, `version: "1.0.0"`, `lifecycle: "supported"`,
+`status: "active"`, `verification.oracle: "tests"`,
+`verification.strategy.primary: "regression"`,
+`verification.strategy.deterministic_check_available: true`,
+`change_policy.breaking_change_requires: ["doc_update", "trace_update",
+"test_update", "human_approval"]`, `test_weakening_allowed: false` e
+`human_approval_required: true`. Os `authority_docs` abaixo usam slugs de
+cabeçalhos Markdown existentes, verificados nesta tarefa com `rg '^#{1,6} '`. A
+ficha RN não é usada como âncora porque não contém cabeçalho Markdown.
+
+| ID               | Domínio  | Tipo / severidade        | Statement CNL                                                                                       | `authority_docs` (doc, âncora)                                                                  | Provenance                     | Verificação e teste existente                                                                                      |
+| ---------------- | -------- | ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
+| `INV-INF-001`    | `INF`    | `lifecycle` / `gate`     | The INF AIT lifecycle MUST keep local finalization as an explicit agent action.                     | `docs/framework/product/domains/inf/teat/APP.md`, `offline-first--doutrina`                     | `APP-TEAT`                     | `unit`; `backend/domains/inf/ait/src/ait-lifecycle.service.spec.ts`; finalização local do AIT.                     |
+| `INV-EST-001`    | `EST`    | `data_contract` / `gate` | EST crash records MUST preserve the BOAT persistent contract within the tenant transaction.         | `docs/framework/product/domains/est/boat/APP.md`, `ciclo-de-vida--visão-geral`                  | `APP-BOAT`, `ADR-0002`         | `int`; `backend/domains/est/crash/tests/integration/boat-contract.integration.spec.ts`; contrato persistente BOAT. |
+| `INV-CH-001`     | `CH`     | `lifecycle` / `gate`     | CH MUST open an encounter only from a checked-in appointment.                                       | `docs/framework/product/domains/ch/pec/workflows/WF-PEC-001.md`, `transições-e-gatilhos`        | `WF-PEC-001`, `APP-PEC`        | `unit`; `backend/domains/ch/encounters/tests/unit/encounter-lifecycle.service.spec.ts`; `AC-PEC-002-1`.            |
+| `INV-OPS-001`    | `OPS`    | `lifecycle` / `gate`     | OPS MUST enforce the pending-queue guard before closing a shift.                                    | `docs/framework/product/domains/inf/teat/screens/IU-TEAT-close-shift.md`, `contrato-transcrito` | `APP-TEAT`, `JRN-TEAT-001`     | `int`; `backend/domains/ops/field/tests/integration/shift-lifecycle.integration.spec.ts`; C-0002-36.               |
+| `INV-PORTAL-001` | `PORTAL` | `state_machine` / `gate` | PORTAL MUST persist the documented request protocol sequence and request lifecycle transactionally. | `docs/framework/product/transversal/portal/APP.md`, `modelo-de-operação`                        | `APP-PORTAL`, `ADR-0002`       | `int`; `backend/domains/portal/requests/tests/integration/portal-requests.integration.spec.ts`; C-0002-30/31/32.   |
+| `INV-DASH-001`   | `DASH`   | `security` / `gate`      | DASH Auditor and DPO access MUST be read-only.                                                      | `docs/framework/product/transversal/dashboard/APP.md`, `atores`                                 | `APP-DASHBOARD`, `RN-DASH-171` | `unit`; `backend/domains/shared/src/policy.spec.ts`; Auditor/DPO dashboard mutation denial.                        |
+| `INV-SEC-001`    | `SEC`    | `security` / `hard-fail` | SEC MUST protect BOAT victim data with reinforced access control.                                   | `docs/framework/product/domains/est/boat/APP.md`, `atores`                                      | `APP-BOAT`, `ADR-0002`         | `e2e`; `backend/app/tests/e2e/policy-routes.e2e.spec.ts`; BOAT victim access.                                      |
+| `INV-AUTH-001`   | `AUTH`   | `rbac` / `hard-fail`     | AUTH MUST enforce the declared policy matrix for RAIT and portal command resources.                 | `docs/meta/adr/ADR-0002-unified-backend-modular-monolith.md`, `decision`                        | `ADR-0002`, `WF-INF-003`       | `unit`; `backend/domains/shared/src/policy.spec.ts`; RAIT and portal policy-matrix suites.                         |
+| `INV-DATA-001`   | `DATA`   | `tenancy` / `hard-fail`  | DATA MUST execute BOAT tenant data access inside the current tenant transaction.                    | `docs/meta/adr/ADR-0002-unified-backend-modular-monolith.md`, `decision`                        | `ADR-0002`, `OD-R19-002`       | `int`; `backend/domains/est/crash/tests/integration/boat-contract.integration.spec.ts`; BOAT tenant transaction.   |
+
+`INV-INF-001`, `INV-SEC-001` and `INV-DATA-001` are intentionally scoped to
+facts exercised by their cited test; the broader AIT-state, SENATRAN and RLS
+controls remain source material for later invariant expansion.
+`tools/verify-senatran-boundary.ts`,
+`tools/check-rls-ddl.ts`, `tools/check-rls-smoke.ts` and
+`backend/database/ddl/20-rls-policies.sql` are deterministic implementation
+evidence, not falsely classified as `trace.json` test paths.
+
+## 3. `trace.json` plan
+
+`law/trace.json` is version `1.0.0` with exactly the nine IDs in §2, once each.
+For each entry, `docs` repeats the corresponding `authority_docs.docs`,
+`code_areas` identifies the cited implementation area and `tests` has exactly
+the existing test path listed in §2, its matching suite and `target_type:
+"test"`. It contains no inferred path, generated digest or assertion count.
+
+`test_corpus` is `[]`. DEVAI discovery currently finds no test file under
+`packages/**/tests/*.test.ts` or `tests/**`; the trace therefore must not assert
+execution, manufacture a digest, or add the backend test paths to `test_corpus`.
+
+## 4. Schema roster M3 and gate rule (a)
+
+The roster is every file matching
+`node_modules/@aarusso-nyx/devai/dist/runtime/index/schemas/*.schema.json` in
+the installed DEVAI `1.5.6` package. TASK-0003 copies each one byte-for-byte to
+`law/schemas/` and writes `law/schemas/manifest.json` with the package version
+and one SHA-256 per copied filename.
+
+Rule **(a)** compares the complete filename set, each copied byte stream and
+each manifest SHA-256 against `--package-schemas-dir`. A missing, extra, altered
+or hash-divergent schema is a violation. The gate does not format, normalize or
+repair a schema copy.
+
+## 5. Provenance gate rule (b)
+
+Rule **(b)** resolves every ID in `provenance` and in `authority_docs` against
+these closed forms and locations:
+
+| Family | ID regex                       | Resolution                                                                                         |
+| ------ | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| RN     | `^RN-[A-Z]+-[0-9]{3}$`         | `docs/framework/product/**/rules/<id>.md`                                                          |
+| WF     | `^WF-[A-Z]+-[0-9]{3}$`         | `docs/framework/product/**/workflows/<id>.md` or `docs/framework/product/shared/workflows/<id>.md` |
+| UC     | `^UC-[A-Z]+-[0-9]{3}$`         | `docs/framework/product/**/use-cases/<id>.md`                                                      |
+| JRN    | `^JRN-[A-Z]+-[0-9]{3}$`        | `docs/framework/product/**/journeys/<id>.md`                                                       |
+| APP    | `^APP-[A-Z0-9]+$`              | a `docs/framework/product/**/APP.md` whose front matter declares the ID                            |
+| ADR    | `^ADR-[0-9]{4}$`               | `docs/meta/adr/<id>-*.md` or `law/adr/<id>-*.md`                                                   |
+| OD     | `^OD(?:-[A-Z0-9]+)*-[0-9]{3}$` | a table row in `docs/meta/knowledge-base/open-decisions-rait.md`                                   |
+
+For a document reference, the gate also requires the path to exist and the
+anchor to match the slug of an actual Markdown heading in that document. It
+does not accept an RN front matter field, prose, or a near match as an anchor.
+An unresolved ID, path or anchor is a violation; `source_pending` is retained
+as text where a source is absent and does not authorize a fabricated ID.
+
+The canonical R-0019 OD registry section is
+`## R-0019 — law-corpus`. It contains these rows:
+
+| ID           | Questão                                                                                                                                                                        | Encaminhamento                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Responsável      | Afeta                         |
+| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------- |
+| `OD-R19-001` | R-0018 planned only the removal of `intentionally empty` from `law/adr/README.md`, while rule (e) also requires removal of `Generated by DEVAI v1.4.5.`.                       | R-0018 remains owner of the README and must remove both phrases before the gate/PR can be green.                                                                                                                 | R-0018 Architect | rule (e), `law/adr/README.md` |
+| `OD-R19-002` | The closed reading list has no existing `*.spec.ts` that directly exercises the repository-wide RLS smoke probe.                                                               | `INV-DATA-001` is limited to the cited BOAT tenant-transaction test; later expansion needs a traced existing test before it can claim broader RLS coverage.                                                      | Architect        | `INV-DATA-001`                |
+| `OD-R19-003` | No headed source in the inspected corpus states the AIT status-token transition or the DASH N3 prohibition. `RN-DASH-170.md` contains the N3 rule but has no Markdown heading. | `INV-INF-001` is limited to explicit local finalization and `INV-DASH-001` to Auditor/DPO read-only access, both backed by headed sources and matching tests. A later expansion needs a headed authority source. | Architect        | `INV-INF-001`, `INV-DASH-001` |
+
+## 6. Obsolete-content gate rule (e)
+
+Rule **(e)** scans every README below `law/` and `product/` that has content. It
+fails on either exact obsolete phrase, with no silent tolerance:
+
+- `Content is intentionally empty until authored.`
+- `Generated by DEVAI v1.4.5.`
+
+### Clarificação C-01-06.1 — placeholder isolado
+
+Um README que contém somente o placeholder gerado é isento enquanto seu
+diretório não tiver outro arquivo substantivo e o próprio README não tiver
+corpo autoral além do placeholder. Essa isenção cobre, no estado atual,
+`law/glossary/README.md` e `product/README.md`.
+
+Quando houver qualquer outro arquivo substantivo no diretório, ou corpo autoral
+no README, cada uma das duas frases passa a ser uma violação da regra (e). A
+isenção não alcança `law/adr/README.md`, pois seu diretório contém ADRs, nem
+qualquer diretório já povoado. C-01-06 e o RED de `OD-R19-001` permanecem
+inalterados.
+
+At contract time `law/adr/README.md` contains both phrases despite existing ADR
+content. This is the expected RED dependency recorded in `OD-R19-001`; it does
+not narrow rule (e), transfer the R-0018 write boundary, or permit a green claim
+before the R-0018 repair merges.
+
+## 7. Gate interface and acceptance criteria
+
+TASK-0005 implements this exact public interface, with repository defaults and
+exit status 0 for no violations and 1 otherwise:
+
+```text
+node tools/law/verify.mjs --repo-root <path> --package-schemas-dir <path> --od-registry <path>
+```
+
+It synchronously exports:
+
+```js
+verifyLawCorpus({ repoRoot, packageSchemasDir, odRegistryPath });
+// => { violations: [{ rule, code, path, detail }] }
+```
+
+| Criterion | Required result                                                                                                           |
+| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| C-01-01   | `CTG-0001.md` is non-empty and defines the M2 policy, nine closed IDs and the trace plan.                                 |
+| C-01-02   | Each M2 client and each `SEC`, `AUTH`, `DATA` entry is active, readiness-bearing and linked to an existing test in §2.    |
+| C-01-03   | Every authority document anchor is a verified Markdown-heading slug; RN provenance is never substituted for an anchor.    |
+| C-01-04   | Rule (a) rejects a missing, extra, byte-different or SHA-different M3 schema.                                             |
+| C-01-05   | Rule (b) rejects unresolved provenance, path, document anchor or OD; `OD-R19-*` resolves in the canonical R-0019 section. |
+| C-01-06   | Rule (e) rejects either obsolete phrase. It remains expected RED until the R-0018-owned README has removed both phrases.  |
+| C-01-07   | The CLI and synchronous export have exactly the interface stated above.                                                   |
+
+The task acceptance commands are `test -s work/rounds/R-0019/contracts/CTG-0001.md`
+and `pnpm format:check`.
